From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_L1436_ENGINE_TRACKED count line counts only pages a CPU mark would untrack

Checker fix to 1008 (port of zortos293/Lichii #1436, 6cd99d2e15, Zortos, from Lucas Borges'
#1161). The "pages P stayed tracked" figure counted every tracked page of each engine write,
also pages an earlier engine write had already marked CPU-modified; the old mark would have
untracked those at that earlier write, so nothing more is saved by the later one. Now only pages
that are tracked and not yet CPU-modified count, so P is the protection changes saved (each
with its undo at the next upload). Count only: no change to what is marked or tracked.
Unset: as T181. KEEPS THE STORE (word_manager.h is not a translation id input).
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/word_manager.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/word_manager.h
index 4576b6dc29..67c44d3819 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/word_manager.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/word_manager.h
@@ -271,7 +271,10 @@ struct WordManager {
             if (hot_pages) {
                 hot_state->clean[index] &= ~mask;
             }
-            kept += static_cast<u64>(std::popcount(~untracked_words[index] & mask));
+            // Only pages a CPU mark would untrack now: tracked and not yet CPU-modified (a page
+            // an earlier engine write left marked would have been untracked by that write already).
+            kept += static_cast<u64>(
+                std::popcount(~untracked_words[index] & ~cpu_words[index] & mask));
             cpu_words[index] |= mask;
             cached_words[index] &= ~mask;
         });
